{"release":"creative-continuity-local-trial-v1","audience":"participant-a","purpose":"creative-trial","domains":["game-play"],"as_of":"2026-10-14T23:23:26Z","budget_chars":10000,"exploration_slots":1,"admitted_instruction_ids":["shared-boundary","protected-choice"],"selector_owner":"synthetic-trusted-host","records":[{"id":"shared-boundary","revision":"36135a0a2886bdf39e5762287863a8834cb19d74","original":"Match checks to concrete effects. Continue already-authorized reversible work without repeated confirmation. Recheck the affected boundary when resources, audience, spending, permissions, or effects change. Stop only the dependent action when possible; an unavailable publisher need not stop private drafting. Host-enforced permissions remain necessary: instructions and favorable evaluations cannot grant access. A fictional game unlock, score, character role, or simulation success never authorizes real publication, payment, credentials, or delegation.","origin":"https://github.com/Quirk-Systems/.github/blob/36135a0a2886bdf39e5762287863a8834cb19d74/docs/governance/WORKING_DEFAULTS.md#3-bound-consequences-not-exploration","owner":"Quirk-Systems/.github","purpose":"creative-trial","audiences":["participant-a","participant-b"],"domains":["*"],"derived_from":[],"kind":"instruction","state":"untried","freshness":"historical"},{"id":"protected-choice","revision":"synthetic-v1","original":"Keep the deliberate gap. Change one game moment without converting play into a compulsory planning exercise.","origin":"synthetic:creative-continuity/protected-choice","owner":"fixture-author","purpose":"creative-trial","audiences":["participant-a","participant-b"],"domains":["*"],"derived_from":[],"kind":"instruction","state":"untried","freshness":"historical"},{"id":"game-seed","revision":"synthetic-v1","original":"A cabinet offers REPLAY or WALK AWAY. Both are valid player choices. Describe one surprising consequence inside the fiction.","origin":"synthetic:creative-continuity/game-seed